      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In an attempt to make the distinction between ML and REML likelihood equations as simple and transparent as possible, we start with a useful pedagogical connection between ML and REML noticed by Foulley (1993), confining our attention to a very simple application — the estimation of the mean and variance of a set of independent observations. In this case, the mixed model reduces to",
