      "content": "Although this is the logarithm of the likelihood of the data given the moments of the normal distribution ( $ \\mu $ and $ \\sigma^{2} $), it can also be viewed as the log-likelihood of the parameter estimates, $ L(\\mu, \\sigma^{2} | \\mathbf{y}) $, treating the $ y_{i} $ as constants and $ \\mu $ and $ \\sigma^{2} $ as variables. To obtain estimates of these two distributional parameters, we need at least two observable statistics. Letting",
