    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "We cannot, of course, know exactly what this bias is because we do not know $ \\sigma^{2} $ with certainty (indeed, we are trying to estimate it). However, the bias is estimable because we have a preliminary estimate of $ \\sigma^{2} $, the maximum likelihood estimate V. Thus, starting with the initial estimate of $ \\widehat{\\sigma}^{2}(0) = V $, a second improved estimate of the variance is",
      "source_page": 795,
      "printed_page": 775,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter27:p005:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        43.0,
        612.0,
        1006.0,
        800.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        795
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          43.0,
          612.0,
          1006.0,
          800.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "57e21ce302a59fe6d07e77d0da36ffe3d891849ff9db4f8fb328a5933ca2fb1e"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_chapter27_formula013]]",
      "source_page": 795,
      "printed_page": 775,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter27:p005:b10"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        336.0,
        805.0,
        698.0,
        885.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        795
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          336.0,
