        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "448a8295468485d8b76b6a72f2cc7b24f9f22be3d12cfbbf68e37422c77a49b7"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "To obtain a solution for this particular example, iteration of Equation 27.6a is not really necessary. However, with models containing multiple fixed effects in the form of the vector u, closed solutions such as Equation 27.6b are not usually possible, particularly in complex pedigree analyses involving unbalanced data.",
      "source_page": 795,
      "printed_page": 775,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter27:p005:b20"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        13.0,
        1390.0,
        978.0,
        1556.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        795
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          13.0,
          1390.0,
          978.0,
          1556.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "c1ae3766af0eb9527bd83824cf376be96075edd559f5a4a4e068112c397dbb89"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In those cases, as we will see below, iterative procedures can still yield solutions that are asymptotically unbiased.",
      "source_page": 796,
      "printed_page": 776,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter27:p006:b2"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        139.0,
        110.0,
        1099.0,
        208.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        796
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          139.0,
          110.0,
          1099.0,
          208.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "65dddb0b72bce3ca0eb8b3e0aa3b972e2e34a6217936c8bfea003f65ea2b3fea"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Note that the REML estimators given by Equations 27.5a and 27.6b were derived under the assumption of normality. That these same solutions can be acquired without reference to any particular distribution (Chapter 2) provides some evidence that REML estimators may often be fairly robust to violations of the normality assumption.",
      "source_page": 796,
      "printed_page": 776,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter27:p006:b3"
      ],
      "bbox": [
